1.175.m:
On the back of that peaked mountain is a lake with fully blown lotuses,
crowded with kāraṇḍava ducks, and adorned by royal swans,
deep like the mind of the virtuous, pure like the mind of the virtuous,
serving many uses, and bringing release to the good, O king;
with fish like severed pieces of cloud, with blooming white water-lilies like stars,
with the great night-lotus like the lord of the night, like a second sky;
where the excellent lotuses were covered all around by honeybees
yellowed with the pollen of full-blown lotuses, as if [made] of refined gold;
where the water and lotuses were hard to distinguish on account of pollen fallen from lotuses
and churned from filaments by swans, swirled about by the wind;
where large lotus leaves, accompanied by drops from clouds shaken down by the wind,
shine by the thousands, resembling pearls;
where lotuses dance, struck by the darting of small carp,
resounding with the calls of noisy cranes and the hum of bees singing aloud;
as if laughing through flocks of swans, as if dancing through waves,
as if chanting through the auspicious cries of kāraṇḍava ducks;
